<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Kibo is a 94-entry table lookup with a menu-bar window. It needs nothing from the system
       but the pasteboard (which the sandbox allows outright) and its own preferences.

       So it runs sandboxed, and the list below is deliberately empty of everything else. There is
       no com.apple.security.network.client and no network.server: with the sandbox on, "Kibo
       makes no network connections" stops being a promise in a README and becomes something the
       kernel enforces — the app could not phone home if a future commit tried to.

       Nothing else belongs here. Adding files.user-selected, Apple Events, or any device
       entitlement would widen what a compromised build could reach, and no feature in SPEC.md
       asks for one. -->
  <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key><true/>
</dict>
</plist>
